### Local configuration ###
# The mail app password, and whatever else a machine needs that must not be in git. The
# template beside it - Config/secrets.properties.example - IS committed, and is where the
# instructions live. Config/config.properties is committed too: it holds no secrets, only
# the environment, the shared QA accounts and the settle timeouts.
Config/secrets.properties

### Generated by the test run ###
# The client's workbook with this run's results and Run links in it. Regenerated at the
# end of every run from the committed import in src/test/resources/testdata, so it is an
# output, not a source. It is about a megabyte of binary: committing it would put a diff
# nobody can read into the history every time anyone ran a single case. The HTML reports
# beside it stay tracked because their diffs are legible.
docs/reports/client_testcase-results.xlsx
#
# Same for the per-feature files: features/ is cut from the import, cases/ holds one results
# workbook per feature. Together about 8 MB of binary, all of it rebuilt from what is already
# tracked. The per-feature HTML under docs/test-cases stays tracked - it is text, and its
# diffs can be read.
src/test/resources/testdata/features/
docs/reports/cases/
